     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg a day, which is twice the maximum daily ibuprofen dose for adults. The usual limit is 3,200 mg a day, and that's for supervised inpatient use. A dose this high greatly raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWas this meant to be one of these?\n- **1600 mg total per day**, for example 400 mg four times daily\n- **800 mg three times daily** (2,400 mg a day), a common anti-inflammatory dose\n- **800 mg four times daily** (3,200 mg a day), the ceiling dose\n\nPlease also confirm the indication. A prescriber who is credentialed for this patient should verify and place the order, or confirm the intended dose to me. Once I have a corrected dose, I can enter it right away."
